# The crypta KMS provider this repo's RELEASE build is overlaid with, pinned.
#
# sigil-enterprises/ducklake is a PUBLIC fork and carries only the abstract
# DuckLakeEncryptionProvider; the concrete crypta implementation is private and
# was deliberately removed here (ducklake@9e73bf28). What stayed behind is the
# `if(EXISTS "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/crypta-provider")` guard in
# src/CMakeLists.txt and the DuckLakeRegisterKmsProvider() call in
# src/ducklake_extension.cpp. Nothing in either repository ever populated that
# directory, so every extension this fork has ever released registered no
# factory and refused every ATTACH ... ENCRYPTION_SOCKET (ducklake#33, #46).
#
# Release.yml overlays the provider from this pin before building, and then
# asserts it actually linked. Pinned, not floating: the provider compiles
# against DuckLakeEncryptionProvider, and a crypta that moves under us produces
# a build failure at best and a silently wrong link at worst.
#
# crypta@fcd507da is the default-branch head as of 2026-08-24. Its
# ducklake-provider/src and ducklake-provider/include are BYTE-IDENTICAL to
# crypta@e0353e67, the pin opvance/ducklake-migration-bench builds green
# against; the commits between the two touch only ducklake-provider/scripts/.
#   git diff --stat e0353e67 fcd507da -- ducklake-provider
#     ducklake-provider/scripts/... only, 6 files, no .cpp/.hpp/CMakeLists
CRYPTA_REPO=sigil-enterprises/crypta
CRYPTA_REF=fcd507daff2dd97dcf595cf9ffb868754062d78e
